# Launch KSP after mod install

When the user indicates **KSP is closed** (or asks for a mod update/reinstall) and you **build and install** KspWebMap to the RSS install, **launch Kerbal Space Program yourself** — do not tell the user to start it manually.

## Default KSP root

```
C:\Users\brand\OneDrive\Desktop\Kerbal\Kerbal Space Program Sol RSS 1.12.4
```

## After install completes

Run in background (non-blocking):

```powershell
Start-Process "C:\Users\brand\OneDrive\Desktop\Kerbal\Kerbal Space Program Sol RSS 1.12.4\KSP_x64.exe"
```

## Workflow

1. User closes KSP (or says it is closed)
2. `scripts\build.ps1 -KspRoot "<path>"` then `scripts\install.ps1 -KspRoot "<path>"`
3. **Start KSP** via `Start-Process` above
4. Remind user to load their save/flight so texture export runs

## Skip launch only if

- User explicitly says not to start KSP
- Install failed
- User is using a different `-KspRoot` (launch that install's `KSP_x64.exe` instead)
